    (
        5,
        6,
        "",
        "I am Yahweh your God",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The Decalogue, take two.</strong> The Ten Commandments appear here in their second canonical form (the first is Exod 20). Differences from Exodus: the Sabbath rationale is the Exodus from Egypt rather than the seven-day creation (5:15 vs. Exod 20:11); the wife and house are reordered in the coveting prohibition (5:21); minor word choices throughout. Jewish tradition resolves the divergence by saying both versions were spoken at Sinai simultaneously — “<em>zakhor</em> [remember] and <em>shamor</em> [observe] in a single utterance,” an idea now embedded in the Friday-night Sabbath hymn <em>Lekha Dodi</em>.",
        "User original",
    ),
