        "But it shall come to pass, if you will not listen",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The covenant curses.</strong> The longest list of covenant curses in the Bible — and one of the most rhetorically intense passages in all of scripture. The escalating intensity (siege, cannibalism, exile, dispersion) parallels Hittite and Assyrian treaty curses of the second and first millennia BCE. The closing image — Israel being sold back into Egypt as slaves and finding no buyer (28:68) — completes a tragic frame: the people who came out of Egyptian slavery returning to it.",
        "User original",
